# Check out JSON and JSONL with LF on every platform.
#
# Several committed data files have their SHA-256 recorded in a manifest (for
# example m3_role_labels/role_labels_v1.jsonl in its provenance manifest), and
# the pipeline hashes JSON artifacts to bind a frozen configuration to its
# inputs. With core.autocrlf=true, a Windows checkout rewrites LF to CRLF, so
# the bytes on disk stop matching every recorded hash while the blob in the
# repository is unchanged. Linux CI never sees the conversion, so the failure
# only appears on a Windows machine.
#
# Every JSON and JSONL blob in the repository is already LF, so this rule
# changes no committed bytes; it only fixes what a Windows checkout produces.
*.json  text eol=lf
*.jsonl text eol=lf
